# What must not be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the important one.
#
# SPEED: node_modules and .git together are the bulk of this tree, and both are
# rebuilt or irrelevant inside the image. Sending them makes every build wait on
# a multi-gigabyte upload before the first instruction runs.
#
# SAFETY: a build context is copied wholesale into the daemon, and anything a
# COPY instruction can reach can end up in a published layer -- where deleting
# it later does not remove it. `.env` holds real database passwords, a live
# Anthropic key and the session signing secret; `dumps/` and `.keys/` hold
# school data and private key material. None of them has any business in an
# image, and CODING_GUIDELINES §12 forbids it besides. The services read their
# configuration from the environment at runtime (see docker-compose.yml).

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets and key material.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.keys
deploy/staging/.env

# School data. 14 MB of restored ERP dump that reaches staging through
# deploy/staging/scripts/load-data.sh, never through an image layer.
dumps

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image; a stale local copy shadowing a
# fresh build is a confusing way to deploy yesterday's bundle.
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
*.log
